  "root_cause_interpretation": "A finite-step kinetic/Peierls-flux weakness when onsite fields are spatially coherent. For the strongest modest-step witness, removing the scalar onsite mean leaves the ratio unchanged, removing all onsite terms retains the failure, setting bond phases to zero removes it at h=.4, and halving hopping removes it. Not explained by an unstable inverse. Circumference-4 uniform-matching commutation is real but the tested geometry-only cohorts do not fail, and correlated-field failures persist on 6x6. These are empirical controls, not a universal theorem.",
